# An allow-list: only what the Dockerfile copies is sent to the build, never a secret.
**
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!loader/**
!pico/**
!pico_finops_agent/**
!plugins/focus/**
!plugins/schedule/**
!deploy/pico-finops-agent.yml

# Never, even inside the folders above
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/credentials.json
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache

# Pico's tutorial data (a demo SQLite and DuckDB, ~16 MB). Only `pico`'s first-run setup copies it, and only when no
# agent.yml exists; the image always has one (deploy/pico-finops-agent.yml), and a missing source is skipped quietly
# (pico/utils/resource_utils.py copy_data_file).
pico/sample_data
